title The debt a run inherits, answered once for the whole ladder
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota row deep-read, send each finished increment.
think Standfast opened clean. The reds ledger guard read 127 rows with no gaps and a headline agreeing with the spine, and the carry meter stood exactly at the ceiling the prior fold left it -- so no red booked the allocation and the constructive queue was free.
think The council rota row was Mars and fire -- cut and stop. Standfast, reds-first, and the three depths of removal read together, and the third named the lap's own shape: a fold is the gentlest depth, since a body lifted into one home destroys nothing and every rung keeps its own name at the door.
think The queue head was taken by measurement rather than off the list. Hashing the family first: eighteen rungs declare meet_the_debt, seventeen share one hash at fifty lines, and the eighteenth differs throughout.
think All eighteen contract symbols already stood public in all seventeen -- debt_standing, meet_of, unmet_debts, met_in, deferred_in, settlement_published, met_bytes, met_answers, meet_refusal, met_note, met_holds, meeting_written, clear_owe, debt_settled, and the four types -- so this fold widened no declaration anywhere, the eighth in a row to need none.
think The stub loop excluded caravan/ladder_checks.rye by name this time, which is the prior lap's lesson applied rather than remembered: a glob that finds the family will find the home the family is moving to.
obs The eighteenth rung keeps its own body, and it is meaning rather than drift. caravan/meet.rye writes the same fifty lines with one difference throughout: it reaches report_out.met directly where the seventeen reach meet_of(report_out).met, because on the meet rung the report IS the meet report and no accessor stands between them. The fourth family running to show that shape -- deem, owe, avow, and now meet -- each a rung whose own subject is the family's subject.
obs Prediction and measurement agree exactly, for the fourth lap running. Realized fall is (identical_copies - 1) x (lines - stub_lines): sixteen times forty-seven is seven hundred and fifty-two, and 79,680 fell to 78,928 -- a fall of 752, which is the number the prior lap's queue estimated from the signature alone.
obs Weighing the next eleven families by realized fall rather than by carried lines reorders the queue. may_pass keeps the lead by carried lines at fifty-one by nineteen, yet its SIX-line signature costs eight lines back in every stub, so it realizes only about 550 -- fifth lap running it has led the printed table and lost the fold. renew_path leads by realized fall at about 720 and stands private in all thirty-one; lost_published follows at about 663 and is already public in every rung, so it is the head that widens nothing.
